        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Mustafa Kemal Atatürk</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1881 CE – 1938 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1881 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaloniki">Salonica</a> (Selanik), <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, as Mustafa; son of Ali Rıza Efendi, a military officer, title deed clerk and lumber trader, and Zübeyde Hanım; a Muslim, Turkish-speaking family that Andrew Mango calls precariously middle-class</span></div>
